# Party banter while exploring the Village of Barovia. Each node opens with an `if` gate: the node is eligible
# only while its condition holds (engine note in docs/regions/village_of_barovia.md §11). Party members speak
# only through interjections; a line plays if a matching member is present.

~ banter_shutters
if visited:village_of_barovia
interject tag:blunt: Count the shutters. Forty-one. Count the open ones. None.
interject tag:cheerful: Maybe they're just shy.
interject class:wizard: Or maybe they've read the same history of this valley I have.
endif
-> END

~ banter_lesser
if flag.ismark_met
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Ismark the Lesser. Mm. Villages name their sons the way masons name stones: by what cracked.
interject name:ilse_varga: He held a house for a month with one sword. That's not lesser. That's understaffed.
endif
-> END

~ banter_locket
if flag.tamsin_locket_recognized
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: Same face, Silvain. Same face. A painting a few hundred years old, and she's sitting in a parlor down the road.
interject name:silvain_aster: Portraits flatter. Coincidences happen. And neither explains why you dream about her, so do keep the locket somewhere I can see it.
endif
-> END

~ banter_bites
if flag.ireena_bite_seen
interject class:cleric: Two bites, and she still keeps her own counsel. Most would be raving by now.
interject tag:blunt: She's a soldier. Nobody told her, that's all.
endif
-> END

~ banter_morgantha
if flag.morgantha_met
interject species:halfling: She pinched my cheek. Like she was checking a melon. Like she was checking a melon for later.
interject tag:blunt: Don't eat anything she sells. That's an order.
endif
-> END

~ banter_pastry
if flag.dream_pastry_eaten
interject class:cleric: Never eat a stranger's pie in a cursed valley. They teach it to novices. I'd have thought it went without saying.
interject tag:cheerful: It was a very good pie, though.
interject class:cleric: That is how they get you.
endif
-> END

~ banter_suspected
if flag.morgantha_suspected and flag.bonegrinder_rumor
interject class:wizard: A windmill on the Vallaki road, ground bone in the crust, and a smile that doesn't move. I have a hypothesis. I don't like it.
interject tag:loyal: Then we stop at that windmill on the way. And we don't knock.
endif
-> END

~ banter_arik
if flag.arik_hollow_noticed
interject name:silvain_aster: The barkeep. There was nobody behind his eyes. Not dull, not simple: absent. I've read of such things. I'd hoped the authors were exaggerating.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Mm. Born without, I think. Pray for him anyway. It can't hurt him, and it might do us good.
endif
-> END

~ banter_aurel
if flag.scholar_notes_found
interject name:silvain_aster: He went up that road with a pen and a map of lit windows. Aurel was the bravest coward I ever knew.
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: Then we'll go and get his pen back for you.
interject name:silvain_aster: That is a ridiculous reason to visit a vampire's castle. Thank you.
endif
-> END

~ banter_raven
if flag.holy_symbol_rumor
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Lost, he said. Not destroyed. Stone remembers where it was put down. So will the world, if we ask it right.
interject name:ilse_varga: Then we ask. Politely first.
endif
-> END

~ banter_spies
if flag.vistani_spies_suspected
interject tag:curious: The Vistani women were counting us. I know counting; I do it for a living.
interject tag:veteran: Then we give them something worth reporting. Make it expensive.
endif
-> END

~ banter_vigil
if flag.mansion_siege_survived
interject tag:veteran: Six of them, two doors, one night. Nobody ran. Good.
interject tag:cheerful: Is that a compliment? That sounded like a compliment.
interject tag:veteran: Don't push it.
endif
-> END

~ banter_doru_destroyed
if flag.doru_destroyed
interject class:cleric: He thanked us at the end. With his eyes. I'll remember that longer than the fight.
interject tag:blunt: He was somebody's son. Now he's nobody's problem. Both of those are true.
endif
-> END

~ banter_doru_freed
if flag.doru_freed
interject tag:blunt: We let a starving vampire out of a cellar. In a village. Full of people who can't run.
interject tag:cheerful: He said he'd go to the castle. He swore. On his mother.
interject tag:blunt: Noted.
endif
-> END

~ banter_hasty
if flag.burial_method == "hasty"
interject class:cleric: We put a man in the ground without a word said over him. That's not a burial. That's tidying.
interject tag:blunt: We were short on time.
interject class:cleric: The dead are always short on time. That's why we're supposed to take ours.
endif
-> END

~ banter_strahd
if flag.strahd_met
interject tag:cheerful: He was taller than I expected. And politer. Why is that worse?
interject class:wizard: Because courtesy costs him nothing, and he wants us to know it.
interject tag:blunt: Next time he stands at a gate, I'm going through it.
endif
-> END

~ banter_strahd_courteous
if flag.strahd_first_impression == "courteous"
interject tag:proud: We bowed to him. I would like it recorded that I bowed ironically.
interject tag:blunt: It didn't look ironic.
endif
-> END

~ banter_gertruda
if flag.gertruda_search_promised
interject tag:loyal: We told Mary we'd look. So we look. Every house, every road.
interject tag:curious: A girl who's never been outside, out there in all this? She'll have gone somewhere beautiful. That's the worst part.
endif
-> END

~ banter_eva
if flag.madam_eva_rumor
interject class:wizard: A seer at Tser Pool who reads cards for strangers. I am a scholar, and I don't believe in fortune-telling. I would very much like my fortune told.
interject class:cleric: Mm. Bring coin. Seers always want coin. So do scholars.
endif
-> END

~ banter_ireena_road
if flag.ireena_in_party
interject tag:loyal: We've got her. Watches stay doubled at night. Nobody sleeps near a window.
interject tag:curious: She's got a better sword than I do. Is that allowed?
endif
-> END

~ banter_death_house
if flag.death_house_sacrificed
interject class:cleric: We gave that house what it asked for. I'll carry that the length of this valley, and further.
interject tag:blunt: We got out. All of us that could.
interject class:cleric: That's the part I'll carry.
elif flag.death_house_children_at_rest
interject tag:curious: The children aren't in the road any more. I keep looking for them anyway.
interject class:cleric: That's right and proper. Keep looking. It's how we remember them.
endif
-> END
